A||||18||87GT||An idiot||||8||
Z||000000||87GT||01-01-2000||06:11 PM||||Well today was a fine day to go get a Haynes book for my fiero so that I could figure some things out about my car.  I went to the local Discount Auto Parts store to get it.  I didnt see it in their racks so I went to the counter to ask if they had any in back.  A younger guy said he thought so and asked an older man to go look.  Anyways, I am standing there with my money in hand and the old man returns with the book and utters, "GM's version of the Pinto."  I said, "Excuse me?" He looked up like he was shocked and I went to say you just lost a sale and to not  disrespect someones pride and joy.(I have never done this before in front of people)  He said he was sorry and all that, but it pissed me off badly.  I went to one of our other 10(sarcastic) local auto parts stores and found it without any crappy comments. ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Patrick||01-01-2000||07:15 PM||||<BR>I would loved to have seen the look on everyone's face when you spoke up. Sounds like a Kodak moment to me! I applaud your decision to speak your mind. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Cooter||01-01-2000||07:24 PM||||As the only male teacher at an elementary school, I really got some strange looks when I drove my Fiero to work. After hearing how unsafe my car was, I started posting articles and pictures outside my room of Fieros that had gone through horrible accidents and the owners survived with only minor injuries. Now they ask where the car is when I don't drive it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||01-01-2000||08:05 PM||||Hey 87GT. It might as well been for a Pinto! The Haynes manual sucks! It steered me wrong countless times in the last 6 months. Get the factory service manual if you can. Check e-bay. Thats where I got mine for almost half of what the Fiero store sells them for. It's coming next week(not soon enough)! If your doing any entailed jobs soon let me know what and if I know, I'll tell you what the Haynes leaves out or differs!||||reg||13
Z||000005||87GT||01-01-2000||09:31 PM||||Hey GoKart, I think I agree with the Haynes manual sucks thing.  I looked to find out where the reverse switch on my car was and it really didnt tell me where it was.  Its kind of confusing.  ||||reg||13
Z||000006||Bill Osmer||01-01-2000||10:29 PM||||I've got all three manuals - Chilton's, Haynes and the Factory Service - all have little bits and pieces missing. I've found that I've needed all three just to get better views or different techniques to do the repairs needed. The Factory Service is the best of all three.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||01-02-2000||12:59 AM||||When I go to the parts counter, fascial expressions tell all. The parts guys never say anything, but I know what their thinking. They just know when to keep their mouth shut. I'm probly one of their best customers. They see me on a weekly basis.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||01:52 AM||||I'm still trying to decide what the Fiero and the Pinto had in common.  Let's see...2 doors, 4 wheels, 4cyl, manual tranny, low center of gravity, ads claim good gas mileage.  Could be a Fiero or Pinto.  Or it could be a Lotus Esprit!  What a bonehead!||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||01-02-2000||01:55 AM||||I think he was referring to the fact that both were publicly prone to catching fire. 'Cept the pinto did do to the placement of the gas tank.<BR>And that the general public views both cars as crap.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Smokey||01-02-2000||04:20 AM||||Those Auto-part counter people are morons. My friend went to get some spark-plugs for his fiero once. You all know him as Silver Bullet. He asked the guy how much Bosch Platinum's would cost, and the guy uttered to himself "too much for that car" Bullet about blew smoke out of his ears yelling at that guy :-)||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||01-02-2000||08:27 AM||||There are some parts counter folks I avoid like they had the plague. These are the ones that need to find a different profession. A few were mentioned above. Other guys at my regular parts haunts I know by name and will stand in a longer line for them to wait on me. These are the guys that when you ask for a Chevy small block 180 degree thermostat, they go straight to the shelf and snag one. They don't ask what year and model car, so they can spend 10 minutes looking it up on the computer and then get the wrong part anyway. They're the ones that ask if you want that needed gasket or seal that you forgot to get because you were messing around with some little gizmo on display at the counter. Yep, there are good and bad auto parts people, but not much in between. I do get more interest from the parts guys when I drive my 36 Ford truck than when I do with my Fieros. Hmmmm.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Gokart||01-02-2000||08:40 AM||||Kind of embarrased to say, but my first car when I was 18 was a Pinto! Never caught fire but I did have to add a quart of oil a day and about half a gallon of anti-freeze! I GAVE it to my younger sister when I joined the Navy and it s..t the bed two weeks later! The guys at my local Autozone love my car. Or they love me! I'm in there twice a week! It's great cause when I need a part the've already got make model year and engine before I even speak!! Maybe I should buy some stock!!||||reg||11
Z||000013||Formula||01-02-2000||11:31 AM||||When I asked for a water pump at my local autozone the guy silently went and got it.<P>He brought it back and checked it out.<P>Then he said "Those are impressive cars aren't they."<P>I just nodded and turned away.  But the next day I saw him driving a blue 87 se v6.<P>So I went in and talked to him.  At first I thought he was being sarcastic but now when I park in front of the store almost all of the salesman look out for a couple minutes.<P>Also, on a sidenote, My friend and I went to the local chevrolet dealership to look at the new monte carlos.  I parked right by the entrance so everyone could see it through the glass doors and windows.  First I noticed some old guy looking at it like he just saw a ferrari and then I saw 3 dealers looking at it.  They were standing at the door.  But the kicker is, when we were leaving every dealer in the showroom was staring out the side windows at me leaving.<P>It must be the wax job.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cooter||01-02-2000||12:14 PM||||My brother has never been a "small car" person. He has a couple of bracket racing cars, a 454 powered 80's Malibu and a 406 powered Nova. He drove my 85 4 cyl car for a while but was not convinced. So when I was getting my friend's 86 GT ready to paint, I took him for a ride. I punched the car from a 3,000 rpm rolling start and when I hit second the GT really smoked the tires. Now he cant wait for me to get my 88 GT's 3.1 engine built and has offered to help with the rebuild. These are great cars, just not very well understood or appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000015||DJRice||01-04-2000||11:11 AM||||I get a kick out of going to the Auto Parts Stores...Last week I went into my local auto parts store to grab a replacement bleeder valve for the brake caliper.  I got that "deer in the headlights" stare.  <P>"You want a <B>meter</B> valve?  What kinda car is it?"  I let him fiddle with his computer, and was pleased to find that those gadgets are offered in the Help! section...<P>HeHe, I bought the "got brains?" bumper sticker while I was there as well.||||reg||1
Z||000016||william_thorniii||01-05-2000||08:10 PM||||Friends,<P>In MI, OH, IN and KY, I have had great luck with Auto Value stores.  They are franchised, so usually they are smaller and dirtier, but they have the real car guys working there.  The way that I figure it, if they can have great guys in a store in Flint, MI, they can and will have great guys everywhere.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||10
Z||000017||JIM GOOSE||01-07-2000||12:57 PM||||Hey, A PINTO isn't a bad car. Had a friend bought one of the first on the market, most basic model with smallest 4cyl (1600cc ?). He drove the thing for years & years with very few problems, an ideal commuter car. If you can find a decent one now, just put a 302 in it and you'll have a great lil streetrod.||||reg||1
