Z||000019||mrfiero||01-07-2000||05:04 PM||||Jim Goose,<P>The early Pintos did have a 1.6 4cyl.  They also could be had with a 2.0 or 2.3 4-cyl. or a 2.8 V-6.<P>I owned a 1976 Mercury Bobcat (an "upscale" Pinto, if you will), and it had the 2.3 engine and a lovely white vinyl roof!  <P>I later dumped it for a '79 Honda Civic, which was dumped for an '82 Civic which was then dumped a couple of years later for an '88 Fiero GT.  I've owned a Fiero ever since April 1990 and will always have one in the garage! <BR> ||||reg||12
